    "result_text": "Green. Here's how I addressed each finding:\n\n**Orphaned exception class \u2014 fixed.** Deleted `rest/advice/DuplicateHouseholdException.java`, which had no remaining thrower.\n\n**Orphaned exception handler \u2014 fixed.** Removed `handleDuplicateHouseholdException` (and its Javadoc) from `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, plus the now-unused `ERROR_DUPLICATE_HOUSEHOLD` constant. There was no explicit import to drop (same package). No stranded support code for the deleted 409 path remains.\n\n**Scope coupling \u2014 confirmed intended, not reverted.** The removal of the household-duplicate rejection is a genuine prerequisite, not an incidental side effect. The acceptance test `coreCapsLevelByHousehold` creates a second owner in the same household (same last name + postcode, distinct telephone, **no** `sharesHousehold`) and asserts a 2xx create; the old `rejectHouseholdDuplicate` rule 409s exactly that case, so the cap rule \u2014 which is defined over \"household members,\" plural \u2014 cannot be exercised while the rule stands. With the rule gone, exact-identity duplicates are still rejected by `rejectDuplicateIdentity`, and an undeclared same-household owner is still surfaced via the existing `possibleDuplicate` flag rather than silently accepted. I've kept the change deliberate and now fully cleaned up after it.\n\nNote: I left the `sharesHousehold` request field in place \u2014 it still has a real effect (suppressing the `possibleDuplicate` flag for declared members), so it isn't dead.\n\nAll tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1).",
